      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "At list LCM zero, every simultaneous solution of an arbitrary decoded congruence system is literally unique."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v27",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v25",
      "href": "tag/GC000C.html?v=481a9a378e54",
      "id": "GC000C",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 2,
      "name": "crt_merge_compatible_prefix_canonical_exists_unique",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 288,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Every arbitrary finite positive non-coprime congruence system satisfying the exact operational gcd-merge invariant has its genuine LCM and exactly one strictly bounded solution."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v27",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v25",
      "href": "tag/GC000D.html?v=481a9a378e54",
      "id": "GC000D",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 0,
      "name": "crt_balanced_bezout_scale",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 289,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Multiplying a subtraction-free balanced Bezout equation preserves all four witnessed natural coefficients."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v27",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v25",
      "href": "tag/GC000E.html?v=481a9a378e54",
      "id": "GC000E",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 1,
      "name": "crt_is_gcd_scale",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 290,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Every common natural scale, including zero, transports the full relational greatest-common-divisor specification constructively."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v27",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v25",
      "href": "tag/GC000F.html?v=481a9a378e54",
      "id": "GC000F",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 1,
      "name": "crt_is_gcd_coprime_factor_remove",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 291,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "A multiplier coprime to the fixed right input does not change the full relational gcd of the left input."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v27",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v25",
      "href": "tag/GC0010.html?v=481a9a378e54",
      "id": "GC0010",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 0,
      "name": "crt_product_witness",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 292,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Every natural product has an explicit first-order value witness without adding multiplication as a new operation."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v27",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v25",
      "href": "tag/GC0011.html?v=481a9a378e54",
      "id": "GC0011",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 2,
      "name": "crt_is_gcd_coprime_product",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 293,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "For coprime natural factors and any nonzero comparison input, the gcd of their product is exactly the product of their individual relational gcd values."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v27",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v25",
      "href": "tag/GC0012.html?v=481a9a378e54",
      "id": "GC0012",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 0,
      "name": "crt_lcm_gcd_cofactor_product",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 294,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "For a nonzero relational gcd, the actual binary LCM is exactly its gcd times the product of the two coprime cofactors."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v27",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v25",
      "href": "tag/GC0013.html?v=481a9a378e54",
      "id": "GC0013",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 2,
      "name": "crt_gcd_scaled_coprime_component",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 295,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "After factoring a common divisor from a multiplier and comparison input, the gcd is exactly that divisor times the gcd of the remaining coprime component."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v27",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v25",
      "href": "tag/GC0014.html?v=481a9a378e54",
      "id": "GC0014",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 0,
      "name": "crt_gcd_monotone_under_divisibility",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 296,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "A divisibility relation between inputs transports monotonically to their relational gcd values with any fixed natural, including zero."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v27",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v25",
      "href": "tag/GC0015.html?v=481a9a378e54",
      "id": "GC0015",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 1,
      "name": "crt_gcd_lcm_distributes_divisibility",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 297,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "GCD genuinely distributes over binary LCM whenever one modulus divides the other, including arbitrary zero inputs."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v27",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v25",
      "href": "tag/GC0016.html?v=481a9a378e54",
      "id": "GC0016",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 2,
      "name": "crt_merge_compatible_prefix_implies_pairwise_compatible",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 298,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "The operational predecessor-LCM merge invariant constructively implies exact pairwise gcd compatibility; the converse is not assumed."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v27",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v25",
      "href": "tag/GC0017.html?v=481a9a378e54",
